    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49484" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŭrĭus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Q. Turius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				12, 26, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> C. Turius, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2, 1, 49</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŭrĭ-ānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a Turius</i>, <i>Turian</i>: hereditas, <i>of Q. Turius</i>, Cic Fam.
			12, 26, 2: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cassia, a peculiar kind so called,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 39, 4, 16, § 7</span></i>
			.</div>
